From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: b53: find the flow accelerator by the chip id

Every BCM47094 has the flow accelerator, whatever its switch revision
(Broadcom's et driver: FA_CAPABLE()). b53 recognised one by the board's
device tree, but an image for a BCM4708 board also runs on the BCM47094
hardware revisions of that board: an ASUS RT-AC66U B1 on the RT-AC68U
image reports chip id 53030 with switch revision 0, as a Netgear R6400
v2 does, and b53 refused the prepended tag there.

Read the chip id from ChipCommon instead, the first register of the AXI
bus, which bcma reports at boot as "Found chip with id". It is read
once and kept.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include <linux/minmax.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
+#include <linux/of_address.h>
 #include <linux/platform_data/b53.h>
 #include <linux/phy.h>
 #include <linux/phylink.h>
@@ -636,6 +637,34 @@ static int b53_port_set_mac_address(stru
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static bool b53_soc_is_bcm47094(void)
+{
+	static int is_bcm47094 = -1;
+	struct device_node *np;
+	void __iomem *cc;
+
+	if (is_bcm47094 >= 0)
+		return is_bcm47094;
+
+	/* The chip id in ChipCommon, the first register of the AXI bus: the
+	 * value bcma reports as "Found chip with id". The board's device tree
+	 * does not tell: an image for a BCM4708 board also runs on the
+	 * BCM47094 revisions of that board.
+	 */
+	is_bcm47094 = 0;
+	np = of_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "brcm,bus-axi");
+	if (!np)
+		return false;
+	cc = of_iomap(np, 0);
+	of_node_put(np);
+	if (!cc)
+		return false;
+	is_bcm47094 = (readl(cc) & 0xffff) == 53030;
+	iounmap(cc);
+
+	return is_bcm47094;
+}
+
 /* The BCM5301x (Northstar) switches with a flow accelerator in front of
  * port 8: switch revision 3 or later, or any BCM47094. As on BCM58xx, the
  * accelerator turns the regular tag into a prepended one on its way to
@@ -644,7 +673,7 @@ static int b53_port_set_mac_address(stru
 static bool b53_has_flow_accelerator(struct b53_device *dev)
 {
 	return is5301x(dev) &&
-	       (dev->core_rev >= 3 || of_machine_is_compatible("brcm,bcm47094"));
+	       (dev->core_rev >= 3 || b53_soc_is_bcm47094());
 }
 
 /* Bit of a port in the CFP port maps: ports 0 to 5, 7 and 8 */
